<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Cemex names Medina as new CFO.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Cemex names Medina as new CFO.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cemex SA, the third largest cement company in the world, said Friday that Hector Medina had been named the company's new chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Medina, who was director general of Cemex Mexico, replaces Gustavo Caballero who died recently. Francisco Garza replaces Medina at the helm of domestic operations, Cemex said.</p>
<p>Cemex is based in Monterrey, Mexico.</p>
<p>-- Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530</p>
